# TDD (condensed)

Laws: no prod code without a failing test; no extra test beyond fail; no extra prod code beyond pass.

Cycle: RED (one behavior) → GREEN (fake / obvious / triangulate) → REFACTOR (green only, no new behavior).

Cadence: minutes. Red too long → split.

Test domain/use-case outcomes via ports. Not private methods, not mock call-order, not E2E as inner loop.

Bug: failing repro first, then fix, leave the test.

Untested code: characterization test → refactor to seams → then TDD new behavior.

Stop: spikes, generated code, ADR/C4 work. Coverage gates = QC (`code-quality-gate`), not this skill.

Python: pytest.raises, fake Protocol. TS: vitest -t, in-memory repo. Go: t.Parallel, table tests after first green.
